IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era25-types`
IMPORT `era25-rules`
IMPORT `era25-goal`

-- Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK) — the encoder's tests. Expected values are
-- worked by hand from the Act.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Goal 1 — statutory sick pay`

-- 80% of £100 is £80; 80% of £200 is £160, above £118.75.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (`Sickness facts` OF 100, Date 2 3 2026, 1) EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (`Sickness facts` OF 200, Date 2 3 2026, 1) EQUALS 118.75
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (`Sickness facts` OF 148.4375, Date 2 3 2026, 1) EQUALS 118.75
-- No lower earnings limit: £50 a week gives £40.
#ASSERT `the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` (`Sickness facts` OF 50, Date 2 3 2026, 1) EQUALS 40
-- No waiting days: payable from the first day, even a single day.
#ASSERT `the first day statutory sick pay is payable for` (`Sickness facts` OF 100, Date 2 3 2026, 1) EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
#ASSERT `the first day statutory sick pay is payable for` (`Sickness facts` OF 100, Date 2 3 2026, 0) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Goal 2 — the unfair dismissal qualifying period`

GIVEN edt IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Dismissal facts`
`started 1 January 2027, dismissed` edt MEANS `Dismissal facts` OF Date 1 1 2027, edt, FALSE, FALSE

-- Six months beginning 1 January 2027 end 30 June 2027.
#ASSERT `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (`started 1 January 2027, dismissed` (Date 30 6 2027))
#ASSERT NOT (`the six-month qualifying period is met in` (`started 1 January 2027, dismissed` (Date 29 6 2027)))
-- From 31 August 2026: six months end 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (`Dismissal facts` OF Date 31 8 2026, Date 28 2 2027, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the six-month qualifying period is met in` (`Dismissal facts` OF Date 31 8 2026, Date 27 2 2027, FALSE, FALSE))
-- s 108(2): one month; (3)-(5): none.
#ASSERT `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (`Dismissal facts` OF Date 1 1 2027, Date 31 1 2027, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the six-month qualifying period is met in` (`Dismissal facts` OF Date 1 1 2027, Date 2 1 2027, FALSE, TRUE)

§§ `Goal 3 — guaranteed-hours complaints`

GIVEN k IS A `Complaint kind`, t IS A DATE, e IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A `Complaint facts`
`complaint` k `triggered` t `, ACAS` e MEANS `Complaint facts` OF k, t, e

-- Trigger 14 March 2027: six months beginning 15 March end 14 September.
#ASSERT `the last day to present the complaint for` (`complaint` `no guaranteed hours offer (27BG(1))` `triggered` (Date 14 3 2027) `, ACAS` NOTHING) EQUALS Date 14 9 2027
-- Trigger 30 August 2027: beginning 31 August, end 29 February 2028
-- (no 31 February; leap year).
#ASSERT `the last day to present the complaint for` (`complaint` `a defective or reduced offer (27BG(2)-(4))` `triggered` (Date 30 8 2027) `, ACAS` NOTHING) EQUALS Date 29 2 2028
-- (8): beginning with the day of awareness, 14 March: ends 13 September.
#ASSERT `the last day to present the complaint for` (`complaint` `other information failure (27BG(8)(b))` `triggered` (Date 14 3 2027) `, ACAS` NOTHING) EQUALS Date 13 9 2027
-- s 207B: ACAS 1-10 June 2027 stops 9 days: 23 September.
#ASSERT `the last day to present the complaint for` (`complaint` `no guaranteed hours offer (27BG(1))` `triggered` (Date 14 3 2027) `, ACAS` (JUST (`Early conciliation` OF Date 1 6 2027, Date 10 6 2027))) EQUALS Date 23 9 2027
-- ACAS 1-10 September: limit 23 September, within one month of Day B, so
-- 10 October.
#ASSERT `the last day to present the complaint for` (`complaint` `no guaranteed hours offer (27BG(1))` `triggered` (Date 14 3 2027) `, ACAS` (JUST (`Early conciliation` OF Date 1 9 2027, Date 10 9 2027))) EQUALS Date 10 10 2027
-- ACAS before the period began (1-10 March): nothing stopped.
#ASSERT `the last day to present the complaint for` (`complaint` `no guaranteed hours offer (27BG(1))` `triggered` (Date 14 3 2027) `, ACAS` (JUST (`Early conciliation` OF Date 1 3 2027, Date 10 3 2027))) EQUALS Date 14 9 2027

§§ `The top-level goal`

pos MEANS `the worker position for` (`Worker case` OF JUST (`Sickness facts` OF 100, Date 2 3 2026, 3), JUST (`started 1 January 2027, dismissed` (Date 30 6 2027)), NOTHING)
#ASSERT pos's `weekly statutory sick pay` EQUALS JUST 80
#ASSERT pos's `first day statutory sick pay is payable` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
#ASSERT pos's `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT pos's `last day to present the guaranteed-hours complaint` EQUALS NOTHING
